-- EXPECT-ERROR: module `Main` imports `Vault` which requires `Cap(IO.Mut)`, but `IO.Mut` is not declared in `needs`
-- Capabilities widening, Task 2 -- Check 4 (transitive `use`), the REJECT
-- side. Companion to accept/t49 with the `needs IO.Mut` line removed.
-- `Vault` (`stdlib/vault.march:26`) declares `needs IO.Mut`; `Main` `use`s
-- `Vault` but declares no `needs` of its own, so `declared_needs = []` covers
-- nothing and Check 4 (`typecheck.ml:5661-5681`) raises an ERROR (not a
-- warning -- contrast Check 1b/1c, which are warning-only for direct
-- body/extern uses; Check 4 is a true error just like Check 1 and Check 5).
-- See core-march-types.md §2.8.6.
mod Main do
  use Vault

  fn main() do
    ()
  end
end
